    <region left="0" top="1377" width="773" height="98" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>B. Small-Signal AC Analysis. Set the source Small signal AC amplitude to 1 V and run an AC sweep.<br />Plot the magnitude in dB and phase of V(vout).<br />Simulation directive: .ac dec 100 10 100k<br />Determine the frequency of maximum output magnitude and compare it with the theoretical natural<br />frequency f0 = 1/(2π√(L1·C1)). Also determine approximately where the response falls by 3 dB<br />relative to its low-frequency gain.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1476" width="772" height="166" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1647" width="329" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Theorical frequency of the maximum output magnitud</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="252" top="1665" width="147" height="149" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1674" width="74" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">L</e>
          <e type="operand">10</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">mH</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="90" top="1674" width="66" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">C</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">μF</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1710" width="229" height="45" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">f.0</e>
          <e type="operand">1</e>
          <e type="operand">2</e>
          <e type="operand">π</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operand">L</e>
          <e type="operand">C</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="bracket">(</e>
          <e type="function" args="1">sqrt</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">kHz</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">1.5915</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1809" width="774" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="774" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>determine approximately where the response falls by 3 dB relative to its low-frequency gain.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="1836" width="150" height="151" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2025" width="645" height="83" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>C. Damping comparison. Change R1 from 68 Ω to 220 Ω and repeat the AC analysis. Overlay or<br />compare the two responses and explain how increasing resistance changes the resonance and damping of<br />the circuit.<br />Important: The SINE definition is used for time-domain transient simulation. The AC amplitude field is<br />used by Small-Signal AC Analysis. These are separate source settings in LTspice</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2115" width="772" height="166" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2304" width="764" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Increasing R1 from 68 Ω to 220 Ω increases the damping because the resistor dissipates more energy, reducing the oscillatory exchange of energy between the inductor and capacitor. Consequently, the resonance peak disappears, and the magnitude decreases smoothly with increasing frequency.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
</worksheet>